    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let's assume\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\vec{v} & =\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\hat{i} \\\\\n& =5 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}+\\hat{k}\n\\end{aligned}$\nand $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}}$\nSo,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\overrightarrow{0} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}} \\times(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}})=\\overrightarrow{0} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}}=\\lambda(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}) \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}+\\mathrm{i}=\\lambda(7 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}) \\\\\n& \\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\overline{\\mathrm{c}}+\\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}=\\lambda \\overline{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot(7 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}) \\\\\n& -29+2=\\lambda(14+40) \\\\\n& \\lambda=-\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{gathered}\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot(-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{k}})+\\hat{\\mathrm{i}} \\cdot(-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{k}})=\\lambda(7 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}) \\cdot(-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\\\ =-\\frac{1}{2}(-14+8)+2=5\\end{gathered}$"
